<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson signs GSM contract in Ghana.</title>
<headline>Ericsson signs GSM contract in Ghana.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group Ericsson said on Monday it had signed a contract for a GSM system within a turn-key project with Scancom in Ghana.</p>
<p>The contract will expand Scancom's GSM network. Scancom is an Investcom Holding SA Company.</p>
<p>&quot;This contract enables Scancom to expand both capacity and coverage as well as add additional services to their network, ie data, fax voice mail and short message services,&quot; Ericsson said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The system will have coverage in Greater Accra, Kumasi and Obuasi and will be in service during October 1997.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
